---
/**
 * About (Despre) — `/despre` · `/en/about`.
 *
 * OWNERSHIP: Workstream A.
 *
 * ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *  THE COMPOSITION IS PRODUCTION-READY. THE COPY IS NOT, AND SAYS SO.
 * ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 *
 * **Required.** IA §2.1 puts `/despre` in the locked sitemap; IA §2.5 gives it a
 * responsibility ("About — trust in architect/practice. *Not:* deep
 * portfolio/service pitch"); IA Step 7's per-page table gives it an entry
 * ("**About (Despre)** — Trust in architect/practice; carries EU-funded
 * expansion narrative … **No dominant CTA**; clear onward paths to Work,
 * Services, Contact"; `DECISIONS_LOG.md` #45, #47); and NAV_DECISION_RECORD.md
 * §4 locks "Despre" as one of four global-nav items. Four components link here.
 *
 * ── WHAT THIS BUILD REPLACED, AND WHY ─────────────────────────────────────
 * The previous implementation rendered a name, an empty statement slot and three
 * equal text links across a full canvas. That was the honest state of a page
 * whose copy did not exist, and it is why it read as a navigation placeholder
 * rather than as an About page: the whitespace carried no information.
 *
 * It is replaced against an **owner-approved visual reference for this page**
 * (supplied 2026-08-11), which is now the authority for composition, density,
 * hierarchy and proportion — the role a HiFi plays for the six page types that
 * have one. `README.md` §"Open questions" still records that About has no Page
 * IA and no wireframe; the reference governs *layout*, and it does not author
 * facts. Where it illustrates content the practice has not stated — a biography,
 * four counts, named software and scanners — that content is NOT transcribed.
 * See `lib/i18n/about.ts` for the four rules the copy follows instead.
 *
 * ── THE COMPOSITION ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   masthead   eyebrow · the locked page name · rule · positioning statement,
 *              against a wide photograph. ~42/58 text-to-image, one band.
 *   01 / 02    who the practice is, beside how it works — a four-movement
 *              sequence, read across.
 *   03 / 04    what it has done, beside what it works with.
 *   closing    one statement, and the two paths the page earns.
 *
 * Two-cell bands, divided by a hairline and opened by a full-width rule. The
 * bands `.bleed` so their rules run edge to edge exactly as the reference draws
 * them; the cells carry the page gutters back, so the type stays on the frame
 * `layout.css` sets. No panel, no fill, no card, no shadow — the ground stays
 * white and the only accent is blue (VISUAL_DIRECTION_v2.0 §1, §2.1, §12).
 *
 * ── DEPTH, NOT REPETITION ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * The Homepage answers "what is this?" — M-1's positioning line, M-2's two-pillar
 * fork, M-3's "small studio with a steady hand". This page may share that
 * vocabulary but must not restate it. So the masthead argues *why the two
 * disciplines are one practice* rather than announcing that they are; §02 makes
 * the working method explicit, which no other page does; §03 and §04 carry the
 * evidence and the capability layer the Homepage deliberately keeps out of M-3
 * ("evidence over claims… never a loud metric row"). The one unavoidable overlap
 * — the practice being small and singular — is reported rather than removed.
 *
 * ── RHYTHM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Still no authored `about` rhythm set, and none is invented (tokens.css). The
 * page composes with `rhythm="homepage"`, changed from the borrowed `service`
 * set: `service` pacing is authored for a single editorial column with 220px
 * quiet beats, and this page is now a dense multi-band composition whose nearest
 * authored sibling is the Homepage. Only the token values change; every section
 * value below is authored against the reference. Swapping to an `about` set when
 * one exists is one prop.
 *
 * ── NO COORDINATE RAIL, NO STATIONS ───────────────────────────────────────
 * `CoordinateRail.astro` scopes the rail to HP, HUB, RC, WE and SV. The
 * reference draws none, the four section numbers here are in-content coordinates
 * rather than a scroll instrument, and the Services index records at length why a
 * rail that measures nothing authored is worse than no rail. `data-station` goes
 * with it — it exists only for the rail tracker.
 *
 * ── MEDIA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Two boxes, both authored as frames with their own `aspect-ratio`, so the
 * layout is identical whether they hold a Sanity image, a temporary visual-QA
 * image, or nothing (`Plate.astro`). There is no CMS field behind either — the
 * same state `Credibility.astro`'s figure is in — so `image` is `null` and the
 * only thing that can fill them today is the `DEV_VISUAL_MEDIA` overlay, which is
 * inert without the flag and cannot survive a build (`verify-no-dev-media`).
 * Both draw from `general`, the pool that claims nothing about either pillar —
 * the precedent Credibility set for practice photography — under two distinct
 * keys, so the two boxes resolve to two different images.
 *
 * ── NO CMS SCHEMA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Unchanged, and deliberately so: no `about` document type, no new field, no
 * content read. IA Step 7 types About "Standalone". Every string is one edit in
 * `lib/i18n/about.ts` away from being the owner's own words, which is the point.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Plate from '../media/Plate.astro';
import ViewTransition from '../ViewTransition.astro';

import type { Locale } from '../../lib/content';
import { aboutMessages } from '../../lib/i18n/about';
import { routePath } from '../../lib/i18n/routes';

interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
}

const { locale } = Astro.props;
const copy = aboutMessages(locale);

/**
 * The closing paths. IA Step 7 names Work, Services and Contact and gives none
 * of them primacy; the approved composition promotes two of them to the closing
 * band and keeps Services as the quiet mono link that closes §04 — the same
 * subordinate treatment `.si-hub` gives the hub continuation. All three paths
 * are present, none is a button, and none is emphasized over the others by size
 * or colour, which is what "no dominant CTA" means structurally.
 */
const onward = [
  { href: routePath('workArchive', locale), label: copy.closing.work },
  { href: routePath('contact', locale), label: copy.closing.contact },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  rhythm="homepage"
  routeKey="about"
  title={copy.meta.title}
  description={copy.meta.description || undefined}
>
  <ViewTransition />

  {/* ── MASTHEAD ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
      Text left, photograph right, both starting on the same line under the
      fixed header. The photograph is `priority` — it is this page's LCP
      candidate and the reference's whole first impression. */}
  <section class="ab-masthead" aria-labelledby="ab-title">
    <div class="ab-masthead-text">
      <p class="ab-eyebrow eyebrow rv" data-rv="meta">{copy.eyebrow}</p>
      <h1 id="ab-title" class="ab-title rv" data-rv="head">{copy.heading}</h1>
      <div class="ab-rule rv" data-rv="meta" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="ab-intro rv" data-rv="meta" data-fixture="about-copy">
        {copy.intro.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ab-masthead-plate rv" data-rv="img">
      <Plate
        image={null}
        locale={locale}
        alt={copy.heroAlt}
        tone="#c9c4ba"
        priority
        devKey="about:hero"
        devPool="general"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── 01 · CINE  |  02 · CUM LUCRAM ───────────────────────────────────── */}
  <div class="ab-band bleed">
    <section class="ab-cell ab-who" aria-labelledby="ab-who-h">
      <p class="ab-num" aria-hidden="true">{copy.who.no}</p>
      <h2 class="ab-section-h rv" data-rv="head" id="ab-who-h">{copy.who.label}</h2>

      <div class="ab-who-body">
        {/* Visibly marked substitute biography — see lib/i18n/about.ts. The
            marker is in the string, not only in this attribute, because an
            attribute is invisible to the person reviewing the page. */}
        <div class="ab-who-text rv" data-rv="meta" data-fixture="about-copy">
          {copy.who.body.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
        </div>

        <div class="ab-who-plate rv" data-rv="img">
          <Plate
            image={null}
            locale={locale}
            alt={copy.who.imageAlt}
            tone="#c6c1b7"
            devKey="about:cine"
            devPool="general"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ab-cell ab-how" aria-labelledby="ab-how-h">
      <p class="ab-num" aria-hidden="true">{copy.how.no}</p>
      <h2 class="ab-section-h rv" data-rv="head" id="ab-how-h">{copy.how.label}</h2>

      {/* An ordered list, because the sequence is the meaning. The connector
          arrow is decorative and belongs to the row above the names, exactly as
          the reference draws it; it rotates rather than disappears when the
          sequence turns vertical, so the direction survives the breakpoint. */}
      <ol class="ab-steps rv" data-rv="meta" data-fixture="about-copy">
        {
          copy.how.steps.map((step, index) => (
            <li class="ab-step">
              <p class="ab-step-head" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="ab-step-no">{step.no}</span>
                {index < copy.how.steps.length - 1 && <span class="ab-step-ar">→</span>}
              </p>
              <h3 class="ab-step-name">{step.name}</h3>
              <p class="ab-step-text">{step.text}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </section>
  </div>

  {/* ── 03 · EXPERIENTA  |  04 · INSTRUMENTE ────────────────────────────── */}
  <div class="ab-band bleed">
    <section class="ab-cell ab-exp" aria-labelledby="ab-exp-h">
      <p class="ab-num" aria-hidden="true">{copy.experience.no}</p>
      <h2 class="ab-section-h rv" data-rv="head" id="ab-exp-h">{copy.experience.label}</h2>

      {/* `data-fixture="statistics"` is the homepage's own marker for a
          fabricated credibility readout (§10.4 discipline), and every label
          additionally carries a visible `(substituent)`. A real value replaces a
          string; nothing here computes, derives or counts anything. */}
      <dl class="ab-facts rv" data-rv="meta" data-fixture="statistics">
        {
          copy.experience.facts.map((fact) => (
            <div class="ab-fact">
              <dt class="ab-fact-v">{fact.value}</dt>
              <dd class="ab-fact-k">{fact.label}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="ab-cell ab-tools" aria-labelledby="ab-tools-h">
      <p class="ab-num" aria-hidden="true">{copy.tools.no}</p>
      <h2 class="ab-section-h rv" data-rv="head" id="ab-tools-h">{copy.tools.label}</h2>

      {/* Plain typographic rows — no logo wall, no icons, no badges. Categories
          rather than product names (lib/i18n/about.ts, rule 3); the composition
          takes authored names verbatim the day the owner supplies them. */}
      <div class="ab-tool-groups rv" data-rv="meta" data-fixture="about-copy">
        {
          copy.tools.groups.map((group) => (
            <ul class="ab-tool-list">
              {group.map((item) => (
                <li>{item}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      {/* IA Step 7's third onward path, deliberately subordinate — see the
          `onward` note above. Same construction as `.si-hub`. */}
      <p class="ab-tools-services rv" data-rv="meta">
        <a href={routePath('services', locale)}>
          {copy.tools.services}
          <span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  {/* ── CLOSING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="ab-close bleed">
    <div class="ab-close-inner">
      <div class="ab-close-say">
        <p class="ab-close-state rv" data-rv="meta" data-fixture="about-copy">
          {copy.closing.statement}
        </p>
        {/* PENDING (C + governance). An empty slot renders no element. */}
        {
          copy.closing.funding && (
            <p class="ab-funding rv" data-rv="meta">
              {copy.closing.funding}
            </p>
          )
        }
      </div>

      {/* A content list, not a `<nav>` landmark: the page already has one named
          navigation landmark in the header, and a second unnamed one would be
          indistinguishable from it to a screen-reader user. The Work Entry's W-7
          and the Service page's S-5 render their onward paths the same way. */}
      <ul class="ab-onward rv" data-rv="meta">
        {
          onward.map((path) => (
            <li>
              <a href={path.href}>
                {path.label}
                <span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">
                  →
                </span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
